---
import PageTitle from "~/components/PageTitle.astro"
import ProsePage from "~/layouts/ProsePage.astro"
import { statuses, simplifications } from "~/data/status"
---

<ProsePage
  title="How the paradoxes are written and checked | Logic Benders"
  description="How Logic Benders explains paradoxes, checks sources, marks human review, and distinguishes settled answers from disputed or unreconciled puzzles."
>
  <PageTitle>How we write these</PageTitle>
  <p>
    Maintained by{" "}
    <a class="underline" href="https://cedmax.net">
      cedmax
    </a>
    . The site owner reviews correction reports and records approval of individual entries.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every argument says what the paradox claims, in two sentences that both seem true. Then it
    says what gives. Where the answer is settled, we say so. Where it isn't, we say that instead
    and show the competing positions.
  </p>
  <p>
    Illusions work differently. Each one shows the effect first, then a way to check it, then
    what is known about why it happens.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-a-paradox-ends" class="display mt-3 text-3xl">
    How a paradox ends
  </h2>
  <dl class="grid gap-3.5">
    {Object.values(statuses).map((s) => (
      <div>
        <dt class="font-bold">{s.label}</dt>
        <dd class="m-0">{s.definition}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h2 id="simplification" class="display mt-3 text-3xl">
    How much we simplified
  </h2>
  <p>Every entry flags where the explanation is simplified, using one of three levels.</p>
  <dl class="grid gap-3.5">
    {Object.values(simplifications).map((s) => (
      <div>
        <dt class="font-bold">{s.label}</dt>
        <dd class="m-0">{s.definition}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h2 id="sources" class="display mt-3 text-3xl">
    Sources
  </h2>
  <p>
    Each entry lists its sources. An entry is published only once its cited sources have been
    checked and its claims brought into line with them. That does not mean every claim is
    undisputed: where experts disagree, the entry says so.
  </p>

  <h2 id="human-review" class="display mt-3 text-3xl">
    Review by the site owner
  </h2>
  <p>
    Source checking and owner approval are recorded separately. A “Reviewed by site owner” badge
    appears only after the site owner has also reviewed the content and marked the entry as
    approved. Source checking is required before that approval can be recorded.
  </p>

  <h2 class="display mt-3 text-3xl">Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    To flag an error or suggest a better source,{" "}
    <a class="underline" href="/corrections/">
      report a correction
    </a>
    .
  </p>
</ProsePage>
